## Why These Fonts?

### Futura Oblique (Authentic Kruger)
Barbara Kruger specifically used **Futura Bold Oblique** in her iconic work. This is THE defining typographic element of her aesthetic:
- Sharp, geometric, modernist
- Oblique (italic) adds urgency, forward momentum
- Bold weight creates strong contrast
- Used in her most famous pieces ("Your Body is a Battleground", etc.)

**Impact**: We now have the REAL Kruger font, not an approximation.

### Josefin Sans (Futuristic Body)
- Geometric sans-serif inspired by 1930s modernism
- Lighter, more futuristic than Helvetica
- Better alignment with "dataimago" AI/data aesthetic
- Excellent readability despite geometric construction
- Subtle Art Deco influence suggests "retro-future"

**Impact**: Body text now looks FORWARD (future AI) while Kruger interventions look SIDEWAYS (critical media stance).

