<file path="ui/src/dataimago-design/packages/css/README.md">
# CSS Package

This package contains the compiled CSS outputs and Bootstrap integration layer for the dataimago design system.

## 📁 Directory Structure

```
css/
├── src/                           # Source SCSS files
│   └── bootstrap-integration.scss # Bootstrap variable mapping
└── dist/                          # Generated CSS files
    ├── dataimago.css             # Core semantic variables (28KB)
    ├── dataimago-icons.css       # Icon system with utilities (8KB)
    ├── dataimago-base.css        # Raw token output (7KB)
    ├── bootstrap-integration.css  # Conflict-free Bootstrap (10KB)
    ├── website-light.scss        # Quarto light theme (3KB)
    └── website-dark.scss         # Quarto dark theme (5KB)
```

## 🎯 Key Files

### dataimago.css
**Core semantic variable system** with theme awareness
- All design tokens as CSS custom properties
- Theme-aware variables with light/dark variants
- Ethical constraints baked in
- Single source of truth for all styling

### bootstrap-integration.css
**Conflict-free Bootstrap integration layer**
- Maps semantic variables to Bootstrap's `--bs-*` namespace
- Eliminates variable naming conflicts
- Ensures reliable theme switching
- Must be imported BEFORE Bootstrap CSS

### website-light.scss / website-dark.scss
**Quarto-compatible theme files**
- Drop-in replacements for legacy 36KB files
- 90% size reduction (3KB/5KB vs 36KB each)
- Imports core system for consistency
- Maintains Quarto's expected structure

## 🚀 Usage

### For Bootstrap Projects (Recommended)

```scss
// 1. Import integration layer FIRST
@import "dataimago-design/packages/css/dist/bootstrap-integration.css";

// 2. Import Bootstrap
@import "bootstrap/scss/bootstrap";

// 3. Your custom styles
@import "your-styles.scss";
```

### For Non-Bootstrap Projects

```scss
// Import core semantic variables
@import "dataimago-design/packages/css/dist/dataimago.css";
```

### For Quarto Documents

```scss
// Use the compatibility theme files
@import "dataimago-design/packages/css/dist/website-light.scss";
// OR
@import "dataimago-design/packages/css/dist/website-dark.scss";
```

## 🎨 Variable Usage

### Semantic Variables (Recommended)

```css
.my-component {
  /* Surface colors */
  background: var(--surface-background-elevated);
  border: 1px solid var(--surface-border-default);
  
  /* Content colors */
  color: var(--content-text-primary);
  
  /* Spacing */
  padding: var(--spacing-md);
  margin: var(--spacing-lg);
  
  /* Effects */
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  
  /* Ethical motion */
  transition: all var(--ethical-dignity-motion-duration-maximum);
}
```

### Theme Switching

```html
<!-- Light theme (default) -->
<html>

<!-- Dark theme -->
<html data-theme="dark">

<!-- High contrast -->
<html data-theme="high-contrast">

<!-- Automatic (follows OS preference) -->
<html> <!-- No data-theme attribute -->
```

## 🔧 Build Process

```bash
# Build CSS from tokens (including icons)
pnpm run build

# Build icon system separately
pnpm run build:icons

# Minify for production
pnpm run build:minify

# Clean dist directory
pnpm run clean
```

## 📊 File Size Comparison

| File | Old System | New System | Reduction |
|------|------------|------------|-----------|
| Light Theme | 36KB | 3KB | 92% |
| Dark Theme | 36KB | 5KB | 86% |
| Core System | 7KB + 2KB | 28KB | Combined |
| Bootstrap Integration | N/A | 10KB | New |
| **Total** | **81KB** | **46KB** | **43%** |

## 🛡️ Conflict Resolution

### The Problem (Old System)
```scss
// Both files define the same variable!
// website-light.scss:
[data-bs-theme="light"] { --bs-primary: #3498DB; }

// website-dark.scss:
[data-bs-theme="dark"] { --bs-primary: #4FC3F7; }
// CONFLICT! Last loaded wins
```

### The Solution (New System)
```scss
// Semantic variables change, Bootstrap mapping stays stable
:root {
  --brand-primary: #3498DB;  // Our variable
  --bs-primary: var(--brand-primary);  // Bootstrap gets stable mapping
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  --content-text-primary: var(--content-text-primary-dark);  // We change
  // Bootstrap still uses --bs-body-color which maps to our variable
}
```

## ✅ Quality Features

### Accessibility
- WCAG AA/AAA contrast ratios enforced
- Focus indicators with ethical sizing
- Touch targets minimum 44px
- High contrast mode support

### Performance
- Single CSS file instead of multiple theme files
- Reduced file sizes (43% total reduction)
- Efficient CSS custom property inheritance
- Minified production builds

### Maintainability
- Single source of truth
- No duplicate definitions
- Automatic theme generation
- Clear semantic naming

## 📦 Distribution

Built files are automatically distributed to:
1. Git submodule consumers via `/dist` symlink
2. CDN via `inst/quarto-assets/`
3. Quarto extension via `_extensions/dataimago/`
4. Development server via `www/assets/css/`

## 🚨 Important Notes

1. **Import Order Matters**: For Bootstrap projects, always import `bootstrap-integration.css` BEFORE Bootstrap
2. **Theme Switching**: Use `data-theme` attribute, not `data-bs-theme` for our system
3. **Backwards Compatibility**: Old file paths still work via symlinks
4. **Minification**: Production builds are automatically minified with source maps
