<file path="ui/src/dataimago-design/README.md">
# dataimago Design System

**Token-first, ethics-enforced design foundation for all dataimago properties.**

> **Modern Sass Architecture**: This design system uses the Sass 3.0 module system (`@use`/`@forward`) for future-proof, maintainable stylesheets.

Treating design tokens like production code with measurable accessibility, dignity, transparency, and equity as first-class "ethical tokens" with CI gates.

## 🎯 Key Features

- **Conflict-Free Bootstrap Integration**: Eliminates CSS variable naming conflicts
- **90% Size Reduction**: Compared to legacy theme files (7KB vs 72KB)
- **Ethical Enforcement**: Built-in accessibility, dignity, and equity constraints
- **Single Source of Truth**: One token definition, multiple output formats
- **Drop-in Compatibility**: Works with existing Quarto/R package infrastructure

## 🏗️ Architecture

This is a monorepo containing the complete dataimago design system:

```
dataimago-design/
├── packages/
│   ├── tokens/                  # Source of truth for all design decisions
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── primitives/     # Base values (colors, spacing, typography)
│   │   │   ├── semantic/       # Role-based tokens (surface, content, brand)
│   │   │   ├── ethical/        # A11y, dignity, equity enforcement tokens
│   │   │   └── icons/          # Icon sizing, colors, states, transitions
│   │   ├── schemas/            # JSON Schema validation
│   │   ├── scripts/            # Build scripts for themes and compatibility
│   │   └── config/             # Style Dictionary configuration
│   ├── css/                    # Built CSS artifacts
│   │   ├── src/                # SCSS source files (bootstrap integration)
│   │   └── dist/               # Generated CSS files
│   │       ├── dataimago.css              # Core semantic variables (28KB)
│   │       ├── dataimago-icons.css        # Icon system with utilities (8KB)
│   │       ├── bootstrap-integration.css   # Conflict-free Bootstrap mapping (10KB)
│   │       ├── website-light.scss         # Quarto-compatible light theme (3KB)
│   │       └── website-dark.scss          # Quarto-compatible dark theme (5KB)
│   ├── icons/                  # SVG icon system
│   │   └── src/
│   │       ├── brand/          # Core dataimago logos (ai_monogram.svg)
│   │       ├── social/         # Social platform icons (github, bluesky)
│   │       └── platform/       # Technology platform icons (netlify, quarto)
│   └── components/             # Component examples (future)
├── tools/                      # Ethical enforcement scripts
│   ├── contrast-check.mjs     # WCAG contrast validation
│   ├── motion-lint.mjs        # Motion dignity enforcement
│   └── prepare-release.mjs    # Distribution preparation
├── examples/                   # Integration examples
│   └── bootstrap-integration-test.html
└── dist/                       # Symlink to packages/css/dist for backwards compatibility
```

## 🚀 Quick Start

```bash
# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Build all tokens → CSS (including icons)
pnpm run build

# Validate tokens against ethical constraints
pnpm run validate

# Run ethical enforcement checks
pnpm run lint

# Build icon system separately
pnpm run build:icons
```

## 📦 Distribution & Integration

### Distribution Channels

The design system automatically distributes to 4 key locations in the R package:

1. **CDN Assets** (`inst/quarto-assets/`)
   - For jsDelivr distribution
   - Includes minified production files

2. **Website Assets** (`ui/www/assets/css/`)
   - For local development server
   - Includes source maps for debugging

3. **Quarto Extension** (`ui/www/_extensions/dataimago/ai-native/assets/css/`)
   - For Quarto document rendering
   - Includes theme variants

4. **Documentation** (`docs/assets/css/`)
   - For package documentation site
   - Includes all theme files

### Files Generated for Distribution

| File | Size | Purpose | Replaces |
|------|------|---------|----------|
| `dataimago.css` | 28KB | Core semantic variables | `tokens.css` + `dataimago.css` |
| `dataimago-icons.css` | 8KB | Icon system with utilities | Inline styles |
| `bootstrap-integration.css` | 10KB | Conflict-free Bootstrap | Manual overrides |
| `website-light.scss` | 3KB | Quarto light theme | 36KB legacy file |
| `website-dark.scss` | 5KB | Quarto dark theme | 36KB legacy file |
| **Total** | **54KB** | **All functionality** | **72KB legacy** |

## 📦 Consuming the Design System

### As a Git Submodule (Recommended)

For R packages and Quarto sites:

```bash
# Add as submodule
git submodule add https://github.com/dataimago/dataimago-design.git ui/src/dataimago-design

# Import in your SCSS
@import "ui/src/dataimago-design/packages/css/dist/dataimago.css";
```

### Direct Import

**Recommended for Bootstrap Users (Conflict-Free):**
```scss
// 1. Import Bootstrap integration layer FIRST
@import "@dataimago/css/dist/bootstrap-integration.css";

// 2. Import Bootstrap CSS
@import "bootstrap/scss/bootstrap";

// 3. Import your custom styles
@import "your-styles.css";
```

**For Non-Bootstrap Users:**
```scss
// Semantic variables with theme support
@import "@dataimago/css/dist/dataimago.css";
```

### CSS Variables Usage

**Semantic Variables (Conflict-Free):**
```css
.my-component {
  /* Surface variables */
  background: var(--surface-background-elevated);
  border: 1px solid var(--surface-border-default);
  
  /* Content variables */
  color: var(--content-text-primary);
  
  /* Spacing and styling */
  padding: var(--spacing-md);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  
  /* Ethical motion integration */
  transition: all var(--ethical-dignity-motion-duration-maximum);
}
```

**Bootstrap Integration:**
```css
/* Bootstrap components automatically use mapped variables */
.btn-primary {
  /* Uses --bs-primary which maps to var(--brand-primary) */
  /* Theme switching works without conflicts */
}
```

## 🛡️ Ethical Enforcement

All tokens are validated against ethical constraints:

### Accessibility
- **Contrast ratios**: Minimum 4.5:1 (AA), 7.0:1 in high-contrast mode
- **Focus indicators**: 3px minimum width, 2px offset
- **Touch targets**: 44×44px minimum size

### Dignity
- **Motion**: Maximum 300ms duration, respects `prefers-reduced-motion`
- **Transparency**: 5s minimum undo window for destructive actions

### Equity
- **Bandwidth**: System font fallbacks, progressive image formats
- **Internationalization**: RTL support, 1.5 minimum line-height
- **Device support**: 320px minimum viewport width

## 📋 Token Categories

### Primitives
Base values that form the foundation:
- **Colors**: Brand palette, neutral scales, semantic colors
- **Spacing**: Consistent spacing scale (4px base)  
- **Typography**: Font families, sizes, weights, line heights
- **Effects**: Shadows, borders, radii

### Semantic
Role-based tokens that map to UI concepts:
- **Surface**: Background colors for different elevation levels
- **Content**: Text colors for different content types
- **Brand**: Brand-specific colors and styles
- **State**: Interactive states (hover, focus, active, disabled)

### Ethical
Enforced constraints for accessibility and dignity:
- **A11y**: Contrast ratios, focus indicators, touch targets
- **Dignity**: Motion limits, transparency windows
- **Equity**: Bandwidth considerations, i18n support

### Icons
Token-driven SVG icon system:
- **Sizing**: Scales from 16px to 120px with semantic sizes
- **Colors**: Theme-aware with platform-specific hover states
- **States**: Hover, active, focus, disabled with transitions
- **Semantic**: ARIA labels and meaningful mappings

## 🎨 Icon System

The design system includes a comprehensive token-driven icon system for SVG logos and icons:

### Icon Organization
```
packages/icons/src/
├── brand/          # dataimago logos (ai_monogram.svg)
├── social/         # Social platforms (github, bluesky)
└── platform/       # Tech platforms (netlify, quarto)
```

### Icon Usage with Quarto
Icons work seamlessly with Quarto's Lua filter that converts `<img>` to inline SVG:

```html
<img src="/icons/brand/ai_monogram.svg" class="icon icon--brand icon--logo-header">
```

### Icon CSS Classes
- **Sizes**: `icon--xs`, `icon--sm`, `icon--md`, `icon--lg`, `icon--xl`
- **Types**: `icon--brand`, `icon--github`, `icon--bluesky`, `icon--netlify`
- **States**: Automatic hover, focus, and disabled states

### R Package Hex Logos
Place `package_hex_logo.svg` in your R package's `inst/assets/` directory for consistent branding across packages.

## 🔄 Development Workflow

### Making Token Changes

1. **Edit tokens** in `packages/tokens/src/`
2. **Validate** with `pnpm run validate`
3. **Build** with `pnpm run build`
4. **Test** ethical compliance with `pnpm run lint`
5. **Commit** changes (CI will run additional checks)

### Theme Support

All color tokens support automatic light/dark theming:

```json
{
  "color": {
    "surface": {
      "page": {
        "light": "rgb(237, 237, 235)",
        "dark": "rgb(20, 20, 16)",
        "description": "Main page background"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Generated CSS includes:
- `:root` variables (light theme default)
- `[data-theme="dark"]` overrides  
- `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` automatic switching

## 🧪 Quality Gates

All changes must pass:
